Third-party components
======================

Nothing in this list is redistributed here. They are named in
main/idf_component.yml and fetched at build time by the ESP-IDF component
manager, so what you get comes from upstream. This file is a map of what the
firmware pulls in and under what terms.

  ESP-IDF                Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  LVGL 9.5               MIT             LVGL Kft.
  TinyUSB                MIT             Ha Thach and contributors
  esp_lvgl_adapter       Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp_lcd_co5300         Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp_codec_dev          Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp32_s3_touch_amoled_1_75c            Waveshare (board support)
  esp_lcd_touch_cst9217                  Waveshare (touch driver)
  qmi8658                                Waveshare (IMU driver)

Fonts
-----
The UI uses Montserrat, which ships inside LVGL under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. No font files are added by this repository.

The clock face draws its digits as seven-segment shapes rather than glyphs,
so it needs no font at all.

Artwork
-------
Every image in main/assets/ is generated by tools/mkassets.py from the
simulator's own screenshots, or drawn by that script. The home background, both
clock faces, and all four planet surfaces are drawn at runtime in code
(main/apps/orb.c). There is no third-party artwork in this repository.

tools/make-orb-texture.py can bake a photograph into main/assets/orb_tex_*.h
and the firmware picks it up automatically. Nothing of the sort is shipped
here, and nothing is fetched for you: pick your own source and satisfy its
licence yourself. The script names public-domain NASA imagery as a starting
point.
